&lt;li&gt;Build and enforce a triage framework for custom client requests: evaluate against platform leverage, sequence against the core roadmap, route to the right owner, and communicate decisions with clarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop a team of PMs spanning benefits, payments, and eligibility/enrollments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in product with meaningful time on benefits, eligibility, claims, or payer systems in a complex B2B2C or healthcare environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years experience managing and mentoring PMs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of scaling an operational product to reliability: you have taken something manual and error-prone and made it run quietly at volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep fluency in how benefits data flows from employer configuration through eligibility verification through member activation, and where it breaks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with claims infrastructure: submission, adjudication, remittance, reconciliation, and provider payments, and a clear view of the highest-risk points in that pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data and instrumentation skills: funnel and reconciliation monitoring, activation analysis, and communicating outcomes to client success, growth, finance, and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on fluency with AI tools as part of how you work today, and a point of view on where AI makes the benefit more reliable at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership: you operate like a founder and do not wait for direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
