&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a technically rigorous and commercially savvy Senior Actuary, Outcomes to bring actuarial depth to Maven&#39;s Clinical Outcomes team. This role spans actuarial modeling, healthcare claims analytics, and client-facing strategy—supporting our Growth and Product functions with projections, retrospective analyses, and value-based care modeling. The ideal candidate brings formal actuarial training or equivalent experience, thrives in a fast-paced startup environment, and can credibly represent Maven&#39;s methodology with brokers, consultants, and employer clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Actuary, Outcomes at Maven, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own claims and savings projections and retrospective analyses across Maven&#39;s employer benefit programs—including performance guarantee assessments, value-based care arrangement modeling, and spend and enrollment projections across Maven&#39;s full program portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and scale Maven&#39;s actuarial and ROI models in Excel, ensuring methodological rigor and integrating models into team workflows for self-service use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct actuarial confidence evaluations to inform revenue recognition decisions and assess financial risk in value-based arrangements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support RFP responses with actuarial projections, benchmarking, and methodology documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform detailed claims analytics for individual and pooled client populations, including evaluation of performance guarantees based on claims data evaluations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join sales and client success calls—including with brokers and benefits consultants—to speak with authority on outcomes methodology, ROI, and actuarial assumptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to thought leadership through white papers, research publications, industry conferences, and partner with Marketing to reach actuarial and benefits audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage external actuarial vendor relationships, serving as owner and subject matter expert on scoping and quality of deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for you to bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An FSA, ASA, or equivalent actuarial credential (or meaningful progress toward credentialing), or a graduate degree with 6+ years of directly relevant actuarial or healthcare analytics experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analysis design, modeling, and data manipulation skills, with the ability to synthesize findings into clear, client-ready outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in both a coding language (SQL preferred) as well as in Excel, and strong ability to use AI to produce and QA code for data exploration and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and comfort presenting to external audiences (e.g., clients), including experience presenting technical material to non-technical audiences&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management instincts with the ability to juggle competing priorities and self-direct in an unstructured environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with healthcare claims data, including medical and pharmacy claims structures, PMPM/PBPM cost modeling, and trend analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for improving maternal and family health outcomes through data-driven innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Helpful experiences and skills (if you don&#39;t have them, you can learn them with us!):&lt;/p&gt;
