&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces for Millennials (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces in Health Care (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast Company Most Innovative Companies (2020, 2023)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces NY (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn&#39;t a vertical-specific role. Maven is looking for an experienced decision scientist who works across the seams—connecting clinical product, member experience, and our AI and healthcare initiatives into one coherent story.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll tie the narrative together: building cross-functional reporting that gives every team a shared view of what&#39;s working and why, and partnering on the data architecture that makes the whole team faster. Instead of owning one surface, you&#39;ll work the connective tissue between them—surfacing insights that only appear when you look across the entire experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re equally at home in the details of measurement and in the big-picture framing that turns data into direction. You know the highest-leverage work often isn&#39;t answering one question well—it&#39;s building the systems and shared language that let everyone answer their own questions better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;As a Senior Decision Scientist, you will:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our key cross-functional reports end to end—understanding not just how they&#39;re built but why each metric matters and how the teams that depend on them make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidate fragmented reporting into a coherent, shared view across clinical product, member experience, and our AI and healthcare work, so every team operates from the same source of truth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface the insights that only become visible when you look across surfaces rather than within a single one, and translate them into clear direction for stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner on the design of scalable data architecture (primarily using SQL and Python), reducing one-off requests and letting every team answer its own questions faster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success metrics with partners across Product, Engineering, and Operations, and pair rigorous measurement with big-picture framing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the shared language, standards, and best practices that make the whole team faster and sharper—mentoring other analysts along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant analytics or data science experience, with a track record of cross-functional or cross-surface work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in SQL, DBT,&amp;nbsp; and a strong background in data visualization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with at least one BI tool (Tableau, Looker)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Python or R&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to design scalable data structures and reporting from both internal and 3rd party sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to juggle long-term, strategic projects alongside ad hoc, urgent requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with a proven ability to turn data into direction for cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with event-based data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of experimentation and/or statistical modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building shared measurement frameworks or semantic/metrics layers used across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
