&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces NY (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a strategic narrative leader to own and evolve Maven&#39;s go-to-market narrative. This role owns how Maven explains itself — to the employers and health plans evaluating our platform and care management programs, to clients demonstrating the quantitative and qualitative value of Maven, and to members navigating some of life&#39;s most important healthcare decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role. You&#39;ll define and maintain the narrative frameworks that anchor everything we take to market: the pitch deck, the positioning, the campaign themes, the launch moments. This is a role for someone who operates at the intersection of strategist and writer — you&#39;re equally comfortable defining the framework and doing the writing yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person is wired for both strategy and execution. You&#39;ve worked at the intersection of consulting-style systems thinking and editorial-quality writing. You move fluidly between strategic framework-building and high-quality written execution. You use AI fluently — it&#39;s woven into how you research, think, and write.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report into the Director of GTM Narrative within the Growth organization, working closely with Product Marketing, Communications, Clinical, and executive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve Maven&#39;s core narrative, ensuring one coherent story that connects employer value and member experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the overarching narrative for major company moments (e.g., new product launches, strategic partnerships, and other defining company moments)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own narrative for existing clients across key moments to drive stakeholder engagement and partnership expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the primary corporate pitch deck and keep it current with product strategy, clinical evidence, and competitive positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Marketing to ensure product positioning lives within a company narrative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate clinical research, outcomes data, and product capabilities into credible stories that resonate with executive buyers and clients alike&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a living narrative system: messaging hierarchy, core value propositions, and usage guidelines for cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build feedback loops with Growth and field teams to understand what&#39;s actually landing in buyer and member conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You May Be a Good Fit If You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 6-8+ years of experience shaping narrative or messaging at a high-growth technology, healthcare, or consumer-facing company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have operated at the intersection of B2B and consumer audiences, ideally in healthcare, healthtech, or another regulated industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are oriented to the close. You&#39;ve built positioning designed to win deals. You understand narrative as a commercial instrument that can transform growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are an exceptional writer who can articulate financial impact to executive stakeholders while expressing clinical rigor and empathy to members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think in systems. You build narrative infrastructure, not just one-off deliverables. You&#39;re comfortable working from data — outcomes studies, utilization rates, financial impact — and know how to turn numbers into a coherent argument, not just a stat in a slide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI and emerging technologies to accelerate research, refine ideas, and scale narrative development without compromising rigor or clarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence cross-functional partners through clarity, credibility, and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn fast and visibly. This role sits at the intersection of healthcare, business, and clinical evidence — you don&#39;t need to know all three on day one, but you need to come in curious and get up to speed quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Candidates May Also Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in management consulting combined with in-house operating experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with go-to-market narrative done at deal speed — turning positioning, packaging, and pricing into language that closes deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthtech or another regulated industry where rigor and accessibility have to coexist&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with messaging work that moved real outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a function or practice from scratch, not inheriting a mature team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
