&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are seeking a Senior Staff Product Designer to completely own our virtual care and provider-facing experiences while driving the evolution of AI-native design at Maven. This role is focused on designing our provider tooling that our virtual care network of clinicians and other providers use during appointments. It&#39;s about identifying the right problems, setting and fully owning the design vision for multiple complex areas, making strategic calls under ambiguity, and leading high-impact initiatives that raise the bar for the team around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll bring deep AI fluency and use it to move faster, explore more broadly, and build more intelligently, while also mentoring others on how to work that way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end experience across complex, cross-functional initiatives for our provider tooling and virtual clinic experience, from early concept through delivery, demonstrating exceptional decision-making and strategic thinking about scope, sequencing, and tradeoffs to drive results across projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how AI should behave in high-stakes contexts: how it communicates uncertainty, when it defers to human care, and how it builds trust with members navigating emotionally charged decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build functional, high-fidelity prototypes using AI-assisted coding tools (Cursor, Claude Code, or similar), and push others to move beyond static mockups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable AI-powered patterns in a healthcare context — confidence indicators, human-AI handoffs, progressive disclosure — that become the standard across Maven&#39;s design system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Product, Clinical, and Data at a strategic level: shaping model outputs into intuitive interfaces, influencing how problems are framed, and driving alignment across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop leaders within the design team and non-design partners, fostering independence, delegating effectively, and promoting leadership among peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve cross-functional tensions, bridging gaps between design, clinical, and product perspectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen community within and outside the design team by championing company-wide cultural initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; You use AI tools daily (Claude, Figma AI, Cursor, or similar) with strong prompting and synthesis skills. You&#39;re also helping others develop that muscle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vibe coding:&lt;/strong&gt; You can turn ideas into working prototypes using AI-assisted coding tools, and you&#39;re comfortable pushing the boundaries of what that looks like in a healthcare context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical depth:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve shipped code to production and can have an informed conversation about backend architecture, model behavior, and system constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic craft:&lt;/strong&gt; A portfolio that shows not just design quality but also evidence of strategic ownership: defining success metrics, navigating ambiguity, and influencing direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve driven complex projects across multiple teams and know how to create momentum without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobile and web:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience designing for mobile applications and responsive web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems thinking: &lt;/strong&gt;Ability to think beyond a flow and communicate a holistic system that can scale for any program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Appetite for complexity:&lt;/strong&gt; Energized by ambiguity and solving complex problems, and comfortable making calls when the path isn&#39;t clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply empathetic toward members and the providers who help them navigate their family building experience, a space that&#39;s emotionally intense, medically complex, and often uncertain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native: you think in terms of what AI makes newly possible, and you bring others along in that thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invested in the people around you. You want the team to be better because you&#39;re on it, and to make the team better by mentoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice To Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare, health tech, or regulated domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working with ML and AI teams on model-driven products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to or building a consumer-grade design system, including Figma variables and advanced component architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
