&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Maven Clinic is the world&#39;s largest virtual clinic for women and families on a mission to make healthcare work for all of us. Through Maven Enterprise, the company partners with more than 2,300 employers and health plans to provide end-to-end women&#39;s and family health programs spanning fertility and family building, maternity and newborn care, parenting and pediatrics, and menopause and midlife — improving clinical outcomes, reducing healthcare costs, and expanding equitable access to high-quality care at scale. Through its consumer platform, Maven provides direct access to virtual care across 30+ specialties, as well as dedicated hormone and GLP-1 care programs purpose-built for women. Founded in 2014 by CEO Kate Ryder, Maven Clinic has raised more than $425 million from leading healthcare and technology investors including General Catalyst, Sequoia, Dragoneer Investment Group, Oak HC/FT, StepStone Group, Icon Ventures, and Lux Capital. Recognized for innovation and industry leadership, Maven has been named to the TIME100 Most Influential Companies, CNBC Disruptor 50, Fast Company&#39;s Most Innovative Companies, and FORTUNE Best Places to Work. Learn more at mavenclinic.com&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An award-winning culture working towards an important mission –&amp;nbsp; Maven Clinic is a recipient of over 30 workplace and innovation awards, including:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TIME 100 Most Influential Companies (2023, 2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Change the World (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CNBC Disruptor 50 List (2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces for Millennials (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces in Health Care (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast Company Most Innovative Companies (2020, 2023)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces NY (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Vice President of Communications to make Maven one of the most recognized, trusted, and culturally relevant brands in women&#39;s and family health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven has spent more than a decade changing how women and families access healthcare. Today, we serve millions of members through employers, health plans, and directly as consumers—and we&#39;re entering a new chapter where the opportunity to build Maven&#39;s brand as one people know, trust, and want to be part of is as significant as the opportunity ahead for our business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Chief of Staff in the Office of the CEO, you&#39;ll lead communications across consumer and corporate PR, social media, executive communications, employer brand, internal communications, and external influence. You&#39;ll shape how Maven shows up everywhere from the &lt;em&gt;New York Times&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;Today Show&lt;/em&gt; to Instagram and TikTok, LinkedIn, industry conversations, and our own company meetings. You&#39;ll turn our products, members, providers, clients, research, data, and point of view into stories that break through; create cultural moments; and build a community of advocates who help establish Maven and its leaders as defining voices in women&#39;s health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a strategic and deeply hands-on role for someone with exceptional taste, instincts, judgment, and writing ability—someone who can see the story before everyone else does and knows how to make it matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maven&#39;s global communications strategy&lt;/strong&gt; across consumer and corporate communications, earned media, social media, executive communications, employer brand, internal communications, and external influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A consumer and corporate earned-media strategy&lt;/strong&gt; that makes Maven part of the cultural conversation around women&#39;s health, fertility, pregnancy, parenting, menopause, weight and metabolic health, and the changing expectations consumers have of healthcare—building relationships across consumer, lifestyle, health, business, technology, and culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communications-led moments and campaigns&lt;/strong&gt; around Maven&#39;s products, research, partnerships, data, members, and point of view that break through, create conversation, and build brand awareness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clinical storytelling&lt;/strong&gt; that turns Maven&#39;s research, outcomes, proprietary data, provider expertise, and member experiences into compelling stories that build trust and differentiate Maven with consumers, employers, health plans, and the broader healthcare community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A customer, member, provider, and partner advocacy engine&lt;/strong&gt; that identifies Maven&#39;s strongest advocates and turns their experiences into earned media, social content, events, peer conversations, case studies, and stories that build both brand and business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maven&#39;s external influence strategy&lt;/strong&gt;, including events and convenings, conferences, speaking opportunities, awards, and relationships with the creators, researchers, policymakers, industry leaders, and institutions shaping women&#39;s health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maven&#39;s organic social strategy&lt;/strong&gt;, building a distinctive voice and point of view rather than simply distributing company news—and understanding how social, creators, executives, members, and earned media can work together to make ideas travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive communications and thought leadership&lt;/strong&gt; for the CEO and executive team, including speeches, media, social, opinion pieces, and major events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maven&#39;s corporate narrative, reputation, and employer brand&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring we tell a clear, differentiated story about what we&#39;re building, why it matters, and what it means to build a career here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internal communications&lt;/strong&gt;, including company-wide meetings, major announcements, and leadership communications that help employees understand where we&#39;re going, why, and what matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A high-performing communications organization&lt;/strong&gt; that moves quickly, has exceptional standards, listens closely to the conversations happening around Maven and women&#39;s health, and measures success by impact—not activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve spent 10+ years building brands and shaping narratives through communications, with leadership experience at a high-growth consumer, technology, or healthcare company—or another environment, such as a major political campaign, where you learned how to shape public conversation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand what makes a story travel, what journalists and consumers care about, and how brands earn attention rather than simply buy it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong media relationships and a track record of generating sustained, high-impact earned coverage through ideas, trends, data, people, and cultural moments—not just announcements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong consumer instincts, regardless of where you&#39;ve built your career. You understand the difference between communicating with an industry and creating something ordinary people notice, care about, share, and remember.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand modern communications beyond traditional media, with strong instincts around social, creators, influencers, podcasts, events, communities, and emerging channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re an exceptional storyteller and writer who can turn a complicated healthcare product, clinical study, business strategy, or cultural shift into a simple narrative people remember.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built executives into distinctive public voices. You&#39;re comfortable challenging and advising a CEO, know when to enter a conversation and when not to, and can capture someone else&#39;s voice rather than imposing your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know how to create moments, not just respond to them—and understand how members, customers, providers, communities, events, and advocates can carry a brand further than corporate communications alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand how to protect a brand as well as build one, with experience navigating sensitive issues and crises with excellent judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re both strategic and deeply hands-on. You can develop the strategy and then rewrite a headline, pitch a reporter, edit a CEO post, or shape an all-hands narrative yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know how to measure communications beyond impressions and press hits, connecting the work to brand awareness, consumer consideration, reputation, advocacy, talent, and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High standards, exceptional taste, intellectual curiosity, low ego, and a bias toward action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Women&#39;s health is having a cultural moment—but the healthcare system still hasn&#39;t caught up.&amp;nbsp;Millions of women are demanding better answers about fertility, pregnancy, menopause, weight, hormones, mental health, and how their bodies change throughout their lives. At the same time, AI, new therapeutics, changing consumer expectations, and a new generation of healthcare companies are reshaping what&#39;s possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven has an opportunity not only to participate in that conversation, but to help define it.&amp;nbsp;We have more than a decade of experience caring for women and families, millions of members, thousands of employer and health plan customers, an extraordinary provider community, a growing body of clinical research, and a rapidly expanding consumer business. That creates an almost unlimited supply of stories worth telling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The opportunity is to turn that foundation into one of the most important and recognizable brands in women&#39;s health.&amp;nbsp;You&#39;ll work directly with the CEO, Chief of Staff, Marketing, Clinical, Product, People, and the broader leadership team to determine how Maven shows up in the world—and build a communications organization capable of making Maven as culturally relevant as the problem we&#39;re solving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role requires active work authorization in the US.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NYC strongly preferred, with regular in-person collaboration at Maven&#39;s New York headquarters and travel as needed. &lt;/strong&gt;Maven embraces a flexible hybrid work model. Our teams primarily operate from the New York Metropolitan area, NY, and remotely via San Francisco/Bay Area, CA, Seattle, WA. For those in our New York City office, we encourage in-person collaboration by requiring team members to work onsite three days a week&amp;nbsp; (Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday). For those based in Boston, DC, Chicago, Seattle, and San Francisco, we encourage in-person collaboration by requiring team members to attend monthly Work Together Days within these cities. This policy aims to balance remote work flexibility with the benefits of face-to-face interaction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;At Maven we believe that a diverse set of backgrounds and experiences enrich our teams and allow us to achieve above and beyond our goals. If you do not have experience in all of the areas detailed above, we hope that you will share your unique background with us in your application and how it can be additive to our teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits That Work For You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our benefits are designed to support your health, well-being and career development, helping you thrive both personally and professionally. We remain focused on providing a competitive benefits package for our employees. On top of standards such as employer-covered health, dental, and insurance plan options, we offer an inclusive approach to benefits:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maven for Mavens: access to the full platform and specialists, including care for mental health, reproductive health, family planning and pediatrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Whole-self care through wellness partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work, in office meals, and work together days&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;16 weeks 100% paid parental leave and new parent stipend (for Mavens who&#39;ve been with us for 1 year+)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual professional development stipend and access to a personal career coach through Maven for Mavens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K matching for US-based employees, with immediate vesting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;These benefits are applicable to Maven Clinic Co., US-based, full-time employees only. 1099/Contract Providers are ineligible for these benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. Maven is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. Maven Clinic interview requests and job offers only originate from an @mavenclinic.com email address (e.g jsmith@mavenclinic.com). Maven Clinic will never ask for sensitive information to be delivered over email or phone. &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you receive a scam issue or a security issue involving Maven Clinic please notify us at: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:security@mavenclinic.com&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;security@mavenclinic.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;For general and additional inquiries, please contact us at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:careers@mavenclinic.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;careers@mavenclinic.com&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Maven Clinic is the world&#39;s largest virtual clinic for women and families on a mission to make healthcare work for all of us. Through Maven Enterprise, the company partners with more than 2,300 employers and health plans to provide end-to-end women&#39;s and family health programs spanning fertility and family building, maternity and newborn care, parenting and pediatrics, and menopause and midlife — improving clinical outcomes, reducing healthcare costs, and expanding equitable access to high-quality care at scale. Through its consumer platform, Maven provides direct access to virtual care across 30+ specialties, as well as dedicated hormone and GLP-1 care programs purpose-built for women. Founded in 2014 by CEO Kate Ryder, Maven Clinic has raised more than $425 million from leading healthcare and technology investors including General Catalyst, Sequoia, Dragoneer Investment Group, Oak HC/FT, StepStone Group, Icon Ventures, and Lux Capital. Recognized for innovation and industry leadership, Maven has been named to the TIME100 Most Influential Companies, CNBC Disruptor 50, Fast Company&#39;s Most Innovative Companies, and FORTUNE Best Places to Work. Learn more at mavenclinic.com&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An award-winning culture working towards an important mission –&amp;nbsp; Maven Clinic is a recipient of over 30 workplace and innovation awards, including:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TIME 100 Most Influential Companies (2023, 2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Change the World (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CNBC Disruptor 50 List (2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces for Millennials (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces in Health Care (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast Company Most Innovative Companies (2020, 2023)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces NY (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven is looking for a VP of Business Operations to own the operating engine behind our core business — beginning with one of the most important numbers in the company: enrollments. This role is accountable for driving member enrollment into Maven’s programs across our core business and, by extension, the revenue those enrollments generate. It also owns three central functions that determine how well the rest of the company executes: AI enablement, central operations, and strategy &amp;amp; operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enrollment is not a single-team problem. It sits at the intersection of nearly every function at Maven, and this role is built for someone who thrives there. You’ll partner daily with Client Success (who own the client relationships that unlock eligible populations), Marketing (member acquisition and lifecycle), Product (enrollment experience and funnel), Finance (targets, forecasting, and unit economics), Data (measurement, segmentation, and attribution), and Clinical and Operations teams. Because so many teams touch enrollment, a core part of the job is holding those cross-functional partners accountable to their piece of the machine — the engine only works when every team delivers its part.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior leadership role with a broad and growing remit. You will build, lead, and develop a multi-function organization — including leaders who own member growth, central operations, strategy &amp;amp; ops, and AI enablement — and you will be measured on what those teams collectively deliver. You set the strategy, define the operating cadence, and raise the bar for analytical rigor across a wide cross-functional surface.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re also looking for someone who can expand the definition of the job. A great deal of enrollment optimization work is already underway, but there is not enough strategic thinking about fundamentally new ways to drive enrollments — approaches that don’t simply depend on securing permission to communicate with a client’s employees. You are accountable for ensuring your team finds and opens those new avenues, and for creating the conditions and analytical foundation that let them do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own member growth for the Core Business:&lt;/strong&gt; Be directly accountable for enrollment targets across Maven’s core business and for the revenue those enrollments drive. Set the strategy, build the plan, and act as a control tower across all cross-functional teams driving revenue to deliver the results quarter over quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and run a scalable enrollment engine:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the full journey from eligible population to enrolled, activated member — spanning client launches, member acquisition and messaging, the enrollment product experience, and re-engagement of eligible-but-not-enrolled members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver AI enablement across the organization:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the function that introduces new ways of working with AI at Maven — and, just as importantly, measures them. Build the adoption playbook, instrument usage and impact team by team, and continuously optimize the value the company gets from how Mavens use AI in their day-to-day work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the central operations team:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the function that enables our member operations and client operations teams to deliver more operationally excellent service. Ensure the systems, tooling, and processes both teams rely on are effective and scalable — built to absorb growth rather than constrain it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the strategy and operations team:&lt;/strong&gt; Own a central strategy &amp;amp; ops function that brings analytical rigor and operating discipline to teams across the org, with specific focus on partnering with Sales, Client Success, and Payer Growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize relentlessly around data:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and consistently iterate on the funnel, and create systems that enable quick diagnoses of opportunities. Build operational metrics that act as leading KPIs for each team contributing to enrollments and bring quantitative rigor into how teams execute against targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hold the cross-functional machine accountable:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner daily with Client Success, Marketing, Product, Finance, Data, Clinical, Payer, Sales, and Operations — and hold each team accountable to its operational KPIs in the enrollment process. Serve as the connective tissue that keeps every part of the engine delivering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instrument and forecast:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Data and Finance to build the measurement, segmentation, attribution, and forecasting needed to know exactly what is and isn’t working, and to forecast enrollment and revenue with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience driving growth, enrollment, acquisition, revenue, or business operations outcomes, with a track record of personally owning and hitting a number — ideally in healthcare, benefits, marketplaces, consumer subscription, or another environment with a complex funnel and multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven people and organizational leadership. You have built and led multi-team or multi-function organizations, hired and developed leaders beneath you, and delivered results through a team rather than solely through your own execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elite quantitative ability as a core competency. You can build and interrogate a funnel model yourself, size opportunities, design experiments, and instinctively optimize around data rather than intuition. Strong quant is non-negotiable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic range across functions. You can set direction for several distinct teams at once — growth, operations, strategy, and enablement — sequence their priorities, and push each toward fundamentally new approaches rather than incremental improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational systems and scaling experience. You have owned the tooling, processes, and systems that service or operations teams depend on, and know how to make them effective and scalable ahead of demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency and conviction. You have a point of view on where AI creates real leverage in a business, and the discipline to measure it rather than assume it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional leadership and accountability. Proven ability to align and mobilize many teams — Client Success, Marketing, Product, Finance, Data, Clinical, Operations — around a shared goal without direct authority over most of them, and to hold each accountable to its operational commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial instincts. You understand how enrollment translates into revenue and unit economics, and you can partner with Finance on targets and forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort in a fast-paced, mission-driven environment with high visibility and direct accountability for a top-line company metric.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $275,000 - $320,000 per year. You will also be entitled to receive bonus, equity, and benefits. Individual pay decisions are based on qualifications, experience, and skillset.&lt;/p&gt;
